    "narrative": "As we approach the final stretch of the season, **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge for Ghost Ride the WHIP with a commanding 81.08 efficiency score. His matchup against R. V\u00e1squez (4.80 xERA) is the gold standard for our lineup tonight; the combination of a favorable SP matchup and a significant dynamic platoon advantage makes **Corbin Carroll** our primary engine for R and SB production. We also see high-ceiling utility in **Brice Turang** (66.27), who benefits from a favorable matchup against Pallante and an 88% stolen base success rate against the opposing battery, making him a critical weapon in our pursuit of the league's scarcest category. **Gabriel Moreno** (67.79) and **Isaac Paredes** (63.82) provide excellent complementary efficiency, with **Isaac Paredes** specifically buoyed by a +10% park factor that pushes his scoring profile well into the elite tier.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card was bypassing **Moises Ballesteros**, whose 44.78 score kept him on the bubble until the final optimization run. While **Moises Ballesteros** offers solid power potential, the combination of facing a high-end arm in Logan Gilbert (3.46 xERA) and a -13% SP skill penalty ultimately relegated him to the bench in favor of the higher-floor production of **Cole Young** and **Griffin Conine**. We are also keeping a close eye on the volatile matchup for **Trevor Story** (49.00), who faces the toughest pitcher of the day in Shota Imanaga (3.63 xERA). While **Trevor Story** remains in the starting nine, his score is suppressed by a negative SP skill adjustment, serving as a reminder that we must monitor for early-game substitutions. As a final note, ensure all lineup alerts are active; with **Gabriel Moreno**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Josh Naylor**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Trevor Story**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Griffin Conine**, **Corbin Carroll**, **Jose Caballero**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Cole Young** all currently listed with pending lineups, any late-scratch announcements will require immediate pivots to our bench depth.",
